export anchor DarkSpreadsheetStyle:
    number: 322
    screen: OpsMonitor
    name: Dark spreadsheet
    idea: The monitor as a dark workbook, with a formula bar, lettered columns and numbered rows holding services, the incident, alerts and deploys as ranges, conditional formatted status cells, floating chart objects and sheet tabs along the foot.
    base: dark
    palette:
        app: #18191c, the page, menu bar and tabs
        grid: #1f2125, cells, chart objects and the style sheet
        header: #2a2c31, column letters, row numbers and chart title bars
        cellLine: #383b42, every cell border
        ink: #e8eaed, cell text
        muted: #a8adb5, header rows, axis and the status bar
        selection: #5aa2ff, the selected cell outline and fill handle, function names in the formula, the request line, the primary button and focus
        selectionFill: #22324a, the selected cell background
        healthy: #7ad99a, Healthy and Resolved text with circle and square on a #1d2e24 cell fill
        degraded: #f2c45a, Degraded and Investigating with triangle and magnifier on a #33291a cell fill
        recovered: #90c2ff, Recovered with a diamond on a #1d2a3b cell fill
        firing: #ff8f86, Firing with an octagon on a #3a2121 cell fill, and the error line
    type:
        Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Arial at 13px and 1.4 for cells,
        ui-monospace, Consolas, Menlo for numbers at 12.5px tabular and for
        the formula at 13px. Range titles 14px at 700, header rows 13px at
        600 muted, column letters 12px at 600.
    layout:
        A menu bar with a green B document tile, Brightwork Ops and
        production last 24 hours read only, and the suite apps at right. A
        toolbar with Refresh, Filter, an Open INC-0427 button and a
        Conditional format status note. A formula bar shows the cell
        reference C5, an italic fx and the formula UPTIME of sync-worker
        over 24h. The work area splits into a scrollable grid and a 380px
        column of chart objects. The grid has letters A to G and rows 1 to
        22. Row 1 is the range title, row 2 the header, rows 3 to 7 the five
        services with Status, Uptime, p95 ms, Queue depth, Down and
        Recovered. C5 is selected with a blue outline and fill handle. Rows
        9 and 10 hold the incident, rows 12 to 15 the alerts with merged
        Condition cells, rows 17 to 20 the deploys, rows 21 and 22 a summary
        of peak, night low, error rate and the spike. Status cells use
        conditional fills plus shape and word. Chart objects have title bars
        with SERIES formulas for requests, error rate and latency. Sheet
        tabs sit along the foot with Overview current and a green underline,
        and a status bar shows the selection. Below 1100px charts move under
        the grid, below 760px the grid scrolls inside its region.
    spacing: A 4px unit. 26px rows, 8px cell padding, 12px around chart objects.
    density: Very dense. Twenty two rows of facts plus three charts on one laptop screen.
    corners: Square cells. 2 to 3px on buttons, chart objects and the document tile.
    borders: 1px cell lines everywhere, 2px under header rows, a 2px blue outline on the selected cell.
    shadows: None.
    icons:
        16px line icons in the toolbar. Status cells use a conditional fill
        plus a filled circle, triangle, diamond, octagon or square, or an
        outline magnifier, with the word.
    focus: A 2px selection blue outline offset 1px with a soft blue halo.
    tone: Workbook terms such as ranges, formulas, Count 5 and Min uptime 99.41%.
